          "text": "# Caffeine Language: Project Overview\n\n## What It Is\nCaffeine is a compiler written in Gleam that generates reliability artifacts from service expectation definitions. It's designed to make declaring service-level objectives (SLOs) and service-level indicators (SLIs) more straightforward.\n\n## Purpose\nThe project aims to simplify how teams define and manage service reliability expectations, particularly for use within CI/CD pipelines. It provides a structured approach to converting expectation declarations into actionable reliability artifacts.\n\n## Key Features\n- **YAML-based configuration** for defining SLOs with threshold values and time windows\n- **Query template system** using the Caffeine Query Language (CQL) for flexible metric expressions\n- **Modular specification framework** supporting basic types, query templates, services, and SLI types\n- **GitHub Actions integration** via a marketplace action for automated compilation\n- **Extensible architecture** documented through RFCs\n\n## Visual & Brand Identity\n- **Mascot**: Features a temporary caffeine icon (250×250px) that suggests an energetic, approachable character\n- **Color palette hint**: The Gleam badge uses pink/magenta (#FFAFF3), suggesting a modern, vibrant aesthetic\n- **Tone**: Professional yet accessible, emphasizing ease of use (\"making service expectation declaration easier\")\n\n## Technical Stack\nBuilt with **Gleam**, licensed under **GPL-3.0**, with 233 commits and active CI/CD testing via GitHub Actions.",
